[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one issue, one fix queued. Read the reports and the tenant they
came from, and #4471 holds three problems. The queued parser fix closes only one of them.

<Callout kind="warn">
Not one issue. Each problem below has its own ticket now. Count each against its own fix.
</Callout>

## The problems

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} {tickets} />

## How they differ

- **`parser`**: the shared parser reads every date month first. A tenant that writes the day
  first gets day and month swapped: a 7 April reminder goes out on 4 July. Every channel, every
  day-first tenant. This is the bug #4471 describes, and the fix that is queued.
- **`hint`**: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field, for tenants that write the
  day first. Their people type what the hint says, and the form reads it the tenant's way. The
  result looks like the parser bug, but it comes only through the booking form of booking-v3
  tenants, and the parser fix does not touch it. The fix is the hint, or the form's reading.
- **`shift`**: the date moves by one day. 12 May shows as 11 May; a client in Lisbon gets
  Tuesday while one in Toronto gets Monday; an invite arrives before the booking. No swap of day
  and month does that. It looks like a time-zone conversion. The desk had already noted these
  reports as one-day moves (`desk-notes.json`) and still filed them by tenant, under the parser.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges on the subject line alone. Subjects
like "Wrong day on the invite" and "Date is wrong" come in for all three problems, so all three landed in #4471. The
intake tag did not help: it is guessed from the reporter's browser, not from the tenant, and it
disagrees with the tenant's cause on dozens of these reports.

## Lessons

- A big ticket can be several bugs that read the same. Before you mark it known, sort a sample
  by tenant and channel, and read the bodies.
- The export comes in overlapping pages: count unique report ids, not rows.

